---
import UtilityWindow from "../layouts/utility-window.astro"
import { SITE_DISPLAY_NAME, getMemberSupportEmail } from "@/lib/site-url"

const pageTitle = `Contact & Member Support | ${SITE_DISPLAY_NAME}`
const pageDescription = `Contact EBC Flex member support for account questions and assistance.`
---

<UtilityWindow title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} canonicalPath="/contact">
  <div class="space-y-8">
    <div class="border-b border-[var(--layout-border)] pb-6">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--layout-text)] tracking-tight mb-3">Contact &amp; Support</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--layout-muted)] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Support channels and account assistance for portal users.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="p-5 border border-[var(--layout-border)] rounded-lg bg-[var(--layout-card)] flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--layout-text)] bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded inline-block mb-3">Account Questions</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg text-[var(--layout-text)] mb-2">Signed-In Account Support</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For account-specific questions, transactions, or document requests, sign in and submit
            your request from the account area. Requests submitted in-portal carry full account
            context for faster assistance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-3 border-t border-[var(--layout-border)]">
          <a href="/api/login-out" class="inline-flex items-center text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)] hover:text-[var(--layout-primary)]">
            Sign In to Portal &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 border border-[var(--layout-border)] rounded-lg bg-[var(--layout-card)] flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--layout-text)] bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded inline-block mb-3">General Inquiries</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg text-[var(--layout-text)] mb-2">Member Services Desk</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For platform navigation questions, access issues, or general assistance, reach the
            member services desk directly by email.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-3 border-t border-[var(--layout-border)]">
          <a href={`mailto:${getMemberSupportEmail()}`} class="inline-flex items-center text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)] hover:text-[var(--layout-primary)]">
            Email: {getMemberSupportEmail()} &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)] bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)] p-4 rounded-md border border-[var(--layout-border)] leading-relaxed">
      When you write, include the best way to reach you and the hours that work for a callback if
      one is needed. If your inquiry involves multiple accounts or dependents, listing them up front
      helps support address everything in a single response.
    </div>

    <div class="text-[var(--layout-text)] leading-relaxed space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)]">Before You Write</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        Many questions are answered fastest inside the portal itself. Account records, status
        trackers, and notices are kept current in the account area, and the FAQ page covers the
        questions that come up most often. Checking those first often saves a round trip.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        When you do need to reach support, including a clear description of what you were trying to
        do and what you saw instead lets the team reproduce the issue and respond with a solution
        rather than another question.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      Support hours and response targets depend on channel volume, but every message is logged and
      tracked to completion. If your question spans more than one topic, listing each item separately
      helps the team answer everything completely in the first response.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      The FAQ page is a good first stop for quick answers, and the Resources section offers deeper
      guides on the topics members ask about most.
    </p>
  </div>
</UtilityWindow>
